From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:08:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Rigid body modes of PETSc: remarks of the review

- the coordinates are given relative to the centroid of the nodes of all
  the processes (PETSc orthogonalizes the rotations against the
  translations in a single pass, which loses accuracy far from the
  origin, and fails the check of a debug build of PETSc);
- the modes are only given to a matrix of the size and of the
  distribution of the finite element space, decided on all the processes
  (an operator of another size is left unchanged instead of an error, or
  a deadlock if only some processes saw the mismatch);
- a PETScPreconditioner given to PETScLinearSolver shares its object of
  PETSc with the solver, which sets its operators: the option
  RigidBodyModes of the preconditioner now applies (it was ignored), and
  the coordinates are computed once;
- SNES with the linear solvers of PETSc converts the tangent operator to
  the AIJ format itself, also on the host, and gives it the rigid body
  modes (MFEM hands this matrix to SNES with its near null space), option
  RigidBodyModes of SNES;
- base types of the matrices compared, unused method removed;
- tests: the preconditioner of PETSc with the solver of PETSc and opposite
  options, SNES with the unknowns ordered by vector dimension; docs: the
  ordering by vector dimension is required (not the default), side effects
  of the block size on the other preconditioners.
